    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d526">

                <pb facs="0528" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/201</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jeffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-03T19:00:00-03:44">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 3, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 4, 12.40
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The French Minister here showed me telegram to-day from the French Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs, quoting the French Ambassador in Washington as follows: “Mr.
                    Polk of State Department advises me that the United States Government is in no
                    position to recommend that French sign an arbitration treaty with Uruguay.” <pb
                        facs="0529" n="357" xml:id="pg357"/> As agreement for arbitration treaty has
                    already been reached between France and Uruguay, I have thought some mistake may
                    have occurred in transmission of this message. Will Department advise me in this
                    connection so that position of the United States Government may not be
                    misunderstood here?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jeffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
